       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppnnmmmmaarrggiinn adds a border around a PNM image.



AARRGGUUMMEENNTTSS
       _p_n_m_f_i_l_e is the name of the input file.  If you don't specify this argu‐
       ment, ppnnmmmmaarrggiinn reads the input image from its Standard Input.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --ppllaaiinn, see
        Common  Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ppnnmmmmaarrggiinn recognizes the
       following command line options:

       You can specify the border color with the --wwhhiittee,  --bbllaacckk,  and  --ccoolloorr
       options.  If you don't specify a color, the program makes a guess.

       The  value  of  --ccoolloorr  is  like  the  argument of the ppnnmm__ppaarrsseeccoolloorr(())
       library routine ⟨libnetpbm_image.html#colorname⟩ .

       The --ppllaaiinn common option was implemented beginning with Netpbm  version
       10.40 (September 2007).

       The --qquuiieett common option is not implemented.


NNOOTTEESS
       To remove a border of a specified size from an image, use ppaammccuutt.  ppnnmm‐‐
       ccrroopp also removes borders, but determines by itself what is border  and
       what is subject.

       For  lower  level  control,  including to add different size borders to
       different sides of the image, look at ppnnmmccaatt.

       If all you're trying to do is get the image up to  a  certain  required
       size, ppaammccuutt may be what you want.

       ppnnmmppaadd does essentially the same thing, but gives you more control over
       the individual margins and does only black and white margins.



